{
  "id": "q-69669",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})=[]+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "958e215bb9ea353d55acb7c0bc8951b85d29dea9d89b00aeb98e7debf70f0180",
      "extractor_sha256": "af03036879151d6bc1d8a980c3dbf01d042d978e39d96a25bdfe63cd50ef1a10",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/958e215bb9ea353d55acb7c0bc8951b85d29dea9d89b00aeb98e7debf70f0180.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $3$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}).$",
      "original_html_sha256": "8df43116ff244ffccc989097cc953119fcf9022ad0886d5bb67747e408d56111",
